    "locked": false,
    "maintainer_can_modify": true,
    "title": "build: explicitly disable cl.exe",
    "user": {
      "login": "bartoli",
      "id": 4445979,
      "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjQ0NDU5Nzk=",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4445979?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/bartoli",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/bartoli",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/bartoli/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/bartoli/following%7B/other_user%7D",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/bartoli/gists%7B/gist_id%7D",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/bartoli/starred%7B/owner%7D%7B/repo%7D",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/bartoli/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/bartoli/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/bartoli/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/bartoli/events%7B/privacy%7D",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/bartoli/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "site_admin": false,
      "name": null,
      "patch_url": null
    },
    "body": "Since 4f1e6de6, cmake for visual studio can only generate projects that use clang-cl.\r\nBut calling cmake without '--preset windows' or '-T ClangCL' still silently generates projects that cannot build anymore.\r\n\r\nFor example, a build with cl now fails in minisketchwrapper.c because we don't pass anymore a cl option to set __cplusplus value properly.\r\n\r\nI propose we explicitly tell at cmake time that this can't work anymore. If not, a lot of windows devs who use cmake without presets will lose time on this.\r\n",
    "labels": [
      {
        "id": 61889416,
        "node_id": "MDU6TGFiZWw2MTg4OTQxNg==",
