      "updated_at": "2026-11-12T10:46:06Z",
      "author_association": "MEMBER",
      "body": "I'm not opposed to this change. However, I do have some concerns.\n\n> I propose we explicitly tell at cmake time that this can't work anymore.\n\nThere are compilers we do not support, yet none of them is explicitly banned. Banning one would make it harder for someone to experiment with it.\n\nFWIW, there is a nightly [build](https://github.com/hebasto/bitcoin-core-nightly#windows-native-builds) that uses `cl.exe`.\n\n> If not, a lot of windows devs who use cmake without presets will lose time on this.\n\nThe documentation should help.\n\nAnyway, I wouldn't want to put Windows devs off merely for the reasons I stated above.",
