      "body": "> > > If not, a lot of windows devs who use cmake without presets will lose time on this.\r\n> > \r\n> > \r\n> > The documentation should help.\r\n> \r\n> In theory, it could be a warning that the compiler is not supported (link to docs) and should only be used at their own risk? However, I am not sure if someone not reading the docs to start will read the warning.\r\n\r\nWell, i was not thinking about someone setting up a new build environement; that person should read the doc indeed. But about the devs that already have a custom build env, and will not read the doc at each pull\r\n\r\n> FWIW, there is a nightly [build](https://github.com/hebasto/bitcoin-core-nightly#windows-native-builds) that uses `cl.exe`.\r\n\r\nIt seems they added patches to workaround the change in the main repo : https://github.com/hebasto/bitcoin-core-nightly/commit/727b9af3e2eb0bffb468e62b217c2f5296bd1690\r\n\r\n",
